WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.6 · Internal Systems & Operations
Finance, procurement and internal controls overview

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Keep money separate and checked from the start, even before you register.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:24.059
Finance systems record and control money: budgeting, bookkeeping, banking, payments, purchasing, income and reporting. Internal controls are the checks that prevent mistakes, fraud and misuse.

4
00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:25.059
Basic controls from day one

5
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:37.500
Separate money: An account or cash box used only for the initiative, never for personal spending. For example: The stall's cash goes in a locked box, counted by two people after each market.

6
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:49.570
Two people approve: Two approvals above an agreed amount; a solo founder asks an adviser to check. For example: The two bakery founders both sign any payment larger than the monthly flour bill.

7
00:00:49.570 --> 00:01:00.900
Receipts and reconciliation: A receipt for every transaction, and records matched to the bank each month. For example: A founder photographs every receipt and matches them to the bank statement monthly.

8
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:13.430
Quotes for big purchases: Two or three quotes above a set amount, noted on file. For example: The bakery gets three quotes for a second-hand mixer and files them with the decision.

9
00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:14.430
Why controls matter

10
00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:18.993
1. Mixing personal and initiative money damages trust fast.

11
00:01:18.993 --> 00:01:24.296
2. Errors found monthly are small; found yearly, they are big.

12
00:01:24.296 --> 00:01:30.600
3. Funders and large customers expect controls and set stricter rules.

13
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:31.600
What they connect to

14
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:37.274
1. Your delegation of authority from Module 3: the same approval limits.

15
00:01:37.274 --> 00:01:42.207
2. Module 9: budgeting, bookkeeping and finance procedures in depth.

16
00:01:42.207 --> 00:01:48.511
3. Procurement: fair choice of suppliers and managed conflicts of interest.

17
00:01:48.911 --> 00:01:49.511
What to avoid

18
00:01:49.511 --> 00:01:53.704
Paying initiative costs from a personal account.

19
00:01:53.704 --> 00:01:57.896
One person approving and making payments alone.

20
00:01:57.896 --> 00:02:04.200
Holding money before you register without checking the local rules.

21
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.600
You describe your finance tools, controls and remaining gaps.

22
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.600
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.200
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
